1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:04,644
Welcome to Tutorial 5:
AI Applications and Scenario Testing.

2
00:00:04,644 --> 00:00:08,510
In the next few minutes,
you'll see what this tutorial covers,

3
00:00:08,510 --> 00:00:12,470
why it matters,
and what you'll be able to do by the end.

4
00:00:13,070 --> 00:00:14,866
Picture a small rural clinic.

5
00:00:14,866 --> 00:00:18,698
Two nurses, one front desk,
and a fax machine that never stops:

6
00:00:18,698 --> 00:00:21,213
referrals, insurance forms, test results.

7
00:00:21,213 --> 00:00:25,105
Then someone says, "There's an AI
tool for that." Could it help?

8
00:00:25,105 --> 00:00:28,140
And how would you know
before you trust it?

9
00:00:28,740 --> 00:00:31,149
Rural health care faces hard problems.

10
00:00:31,149 --> 00:00:34,361
Nearly one in five Americans
lives in a rural area,

11
00:00:34,361 --> 00:00:38,191
where there are fewer doctors
and many hospitals have closed.

12
00:00:38,191 --> 00:00:41,279
AI could help stretch
scarce staff and expertise.

13
00:00:41,279 --> 00:00:46,250
Used carelessly, it could also widen
the gap between rural and city care.

14
00:00:46,850 --> 00:00:49,094
The tutorial has five short sections.

15
00:00:49,094 --> 00:00:51,988
Each one has a video like this,
a short reading,

16
00:00:51,988 --> 00:00:54,750
and a quiz to check your understanding.

17
00:00:55,350 --> 00:00:57,397
Section one explains what AI is.

18
00:00:57,397 --> 00:01:01,118
It learns patterns from examples,
then predicts or creates,

19
00:01:01,118 --> 00:01:03,474
and it comes with four warning signs.

20
00:01:03,474 --> 00:01:07,071
Section two shows what makes
rural health care different,

21
00:01:07,071 --> 00:01:10,510
and why those differences
matter for technology.

22
00:01:11,110 --> 00:01:14,896
Section three looks at where AI
in rural health stands today.

23
00:01:14,896 --> 00:01:17,767
Rural hospitals use it
less and check it less,

24
00:01:17,767 --> 00:01:21,492
and many tools were built with
patients from somewhere else.

25
00:01:21,492 --> 00:01:24,668
That's why this tutorial
is about scenario testing:

26
00:01:24,668 --> 00:01:27,416
trying a tool on realistic
local situations,

27
00:01:27,416 --> 00:01:30,870
including messy ones,
before anyone relies on it.

28
00:01:31,470 --> 00:01:35,277
Section four covers data:
which data are safe to use with AI,

29
00:01:35,277 --> 00:01:39,822
and which never are, like real patient
records. Section five is hands-on.

30
00:01:39,822 --> 00:01:42,462
Even if you've never used an AI assistant,

31
00:01:42,462 --> 00:01:47,068
you'll get started with the free version
of Gemini, Google's AI assistant,

32
00:01:47,068 --> 00:01:50,568
and practice four habits:
ask clearly, check the answer,

33
00:01:50,568 --> 00:01:53,670
protect privacy,
and test before you trust.

34
00:01:54,270 --> 00:01:58,231
By the end, you'll be able to
explain what AI can and can't do,

35
00:01:58,231 --> 00:02:02,379
describe the rural picture,
and use an AI tool with good judgment.

36
00:02:02,379 --> 00:02:06,740
No coding, and no background in
health or computing, is needed.

37
00:02:07,340 --> 00:02:09,320
Let's begin with section one.
